<title>EGYPT: Egypt's Banque du Caire raises 95/96 profits.</title>
<headline>Egypt's Banque du Caire raises 95/96 profits.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egyptian state-owned Banque du Caire said on Monday it raised net profits for the 1995/96 financial year to 70 million pounds ($21 million) from 55 million in the previous year.</p>
<p>The financial years end on June 30.</p>
<p>The bank said in published results customer deposits rose in 1995/96 to 21.24 billion pounds from 20.42 billion. Total 1995/96 income was also higher at 2.69 billion from 2.46 billion in 1994/95.</p>
<p>The bank is one of four main merchant banks run by the state.</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +202 578 3290/1</p>
